{
  "$comment": "What each Black 4 plugin needs from Buzz's plugin API, derived from plugins/*/plugin.js and manifest.json. check.mjs verifies it against a block/buzz-app checkout. Paths start at the plugin's ctx (cordis Context). Path syntax: .name is a property, (n) is the n-th argument of a call, => is what a call returns (a Promise is unwrapped), [] is an array element. 'uses' must exist. 'provides' lists the keys of an object the plugin hands to Buzz: each key must still exist there, and Buzz must not require a key the plugin does not give. 'accepts' is a literal value the plugin passes that the type must still allow. When you change what a plugin uses, change this file in the same commit: tests/canary-contract.test.mjs fails otherwise.",
  "recordedAgainst": "block/buzz-app v1.0.2, the Buzz release installed when this was written (2026-11-14)",
  "envelope": {
    "$comment": "Libraries whose types are part of the plugin envelope. Buzz's package.json must still name these versions; otherwise ctx.effect and React props were checked against the wrong library.",
    "@deepseek-ai/cordis": "4.0.2",
    "@types/react": "19"
  },
